   "plain_text": "### Step 3: Try $ g(n) = 1 $ for all $ n $ Then: $$ g(2m + 2n) = 1, \\quad g(m)^{2021^2} g(n)^{2021^2} = 1^{2021^2} \\cdot 1^{2021^2} = 1 $$ So this works. Then: $$ f(n) = g(n)^{2021} = 1^{2021} = 1 $$ Thus, $ f(n) = 1 $ is a solution. --- ### Step 4: Uniqueness"
