   "plain_text": "$$ f(2m + 2n) = c^{\\alpha(2m + 2n)} = f(m)^{2021} f(n)^{2021} = (c^{\\alpha(m)})^{2021} (c^{\\alpha(n)})^{2021} = c^{2021\\alpha(m) + 2021\\alpha(n)} $$ So: $$ \\alpha(2m + 2n) = 2021(\\alpha(m) + \\alpha(n)) $$ This is a recursive functional equation. It implies that $ \\alpha(n) $ must be linear in the binary representation of $ n $. This is possible only if $ \\alpha(n) = k \\cdot \\log_2 n $, which is not in $ \\mathbb{Z}_{&gt;0} $ unless $ k = 0 $."
